        <h3>Case fatality rate</h3>
        <p>Every widget on this page treats "recovered" as one single outcome. Real outbreaks track a case fatality rate too — the share of diagnosed cases who don't recover — and it's a measure of severity, not just spread: a low-R0 disease with a high fatality rate can matter more than a high-R0 one that barely makes anyone sick.</p>
        <p class="think-links">Further reading: <a href="https://www.who.int/news-room/commentaries/detail/estimating-mortality-from-covid-19">WHO, "Estimating mortality from COVID-19"</a> · <a href="https://archive.cdc.gov/www_cdc_gov/csels/dsepd/ss1978/lesson3/section3.html">CDC, Principles of Epidemiology, Lesson 3</a></p>
