        <p>The moment someone catches this disease, this simulation shows them as orange straight away. Real infections often have a gap between exposure and symptoms — the incubation period — during which someone can look and feel fine while already contagious, which is exactly what makes contact tracing so much harder than isolating the visibly sick.</p>
